==English==
[[Image:Mineral_Mica_moscovita_GDFL107.jpg|thumb|Muscovite]]
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
In 1850 from ''[[Muscovy glass]]'' {{suffix||ite|lang=en}}, from the province Muscovy in [[Russia]]. Named by James Dwight Dana.<ref>Richard V. Gaines, H. Catherine W. Skinner, Eugene E. Foord, Brian Mason, and Abraham Rosenzweig: ''Dana's new mineralogy'', John Wiley & Sons, 1997</ref>

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{context|mineralogy|lang=en}} A pale brown [[mineral]] of the [[mica]] group, being a basic [[potassium]] [[aluminosilicate]] with the [[chemical formula]] [[potassium|K]][[aluminum|Al]]<sub>2</sub>([[silicon|Si]]<sub>3</sub>Al)[[oxygen|O]]<sub>10</sub>(O[[hydrogen|H]],[[fluorine|F]])<sub>2</sub>; used as an [[electrical]] [[insulator]] etc.

